# Fix Component Issues Helper

## File Purpose

This file provides standardized patterns and workflows for fixing common React component issues in the front-end workflow. It should be consulted when:

- Component implementation encounters errors
- Component has TypeScript type issues
- Component rendering is incorrect
- Component performance needs improvement
- Component has accessibility issues
- Component has integration problems with other components

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains component issue resolution guidance and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter in message-commands:

```
fix-component-issues: @parameters/front-end/helpers/recovery/fix-component-issues.mdc
```

For more general recovery guidance, see:
- `recover-implementation.md`: General implementation recovery
- `recover-from-errors.md`: Error-specific recovery strategies

## Component Issue Resolution Process

### 1. Identify Component Issues

Begin by identifying the specific issues affecting the component:

```typescript
// 1. Check TypeScript errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run type-check -- --pretty", false, false)

// 2. Check linting errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run lint -- front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx", false, false)

// 3. Check console errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run dev", false, true)

// 4. Check test failures
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm test -- --findRelatedTests src/components/[ComponentName].tsx", false, false)

// 5. Check component code for potential issues
grep_search("TODO|FIXME|@ts-ignore", false, "front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx")
grep_search("undefined|null|NaN", false, "front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx")
```

### 2. Analyze Component Structure

Analyze the component structure to understand its design and potential issues:

```typescript
// 1. Read component implementation
read_file("front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 2. Analyze component props
grep_search("interface.*Props|type.*Props", true, "front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx")

// 3. Check component dependencies
grep_search("import.*from", false, "front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx")

// 4. Examine component usage
grep_search("import.*[ComponentName]", false, "front-end/src/**/*.tsx")
grep_search("<[ComponentName]", false, "front-end/src/**/*.tsx")

// 5. Check component hooks
grep_search("use[A-Z]|useState|useEffect|useContext", false, "front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx")
```

### 3. Fix Common Component Issues

Apply fixes for identified issues based on their type:

#### TypeScript Type Issues

```typescript
// 1. Fix prop interface issues
edit_file("front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx",
          "Fix component prop type issues",
          "// ... existing code ...

/**
 * Props for the [ComponentName] component
 */
export interface [ComponentName]Props {
  // Fixed prop type: Added proper type definition
  data: Array<{
    id: string;
    name: string;
    value: number;
  }>;
  
  // Fixed prop type: Made optional with default in component
  onSelect?: (id: string) => void;
  
  // Fixed prop type: Added proper generic type
  options: Record<string, unknown>;
}

// ... existing code ...")

// 2. Fix component implementation type issues
edit_file("front-end/src/components/[ComponentName].tsx",
          "Fix component implementation type issues",
          "// ... existing code ...

// Fixed: Added proper type annotation
const [selectedItem, setSelectedItem] = useState<string | null>(null);

// Fixed: Added type guard for nullable value
const handleSelection = (item: ItemType | null) => {
  if (item === null) {
    return;
  }
  
  setSelectedItem(item.id);
  
  // Fixed: Added null check for optional callback
  if (onSelect) {
    onSelect(item.id);
  }
};

// ... existing code ...")
```

