## Common Component Issues and Fixes

### TypeScript Issues

| Issue | Fix Pattern |
|-------|-------------|
| Missing prop types | Add proper interface or type definition |
| Any type usage | Replace with specific types or generics |
| Optional prop handling | Add proper `?` modifier and null checks |
| Type assertions | Replace with proper type guards |
| Generic component types | Add proper generic type parameters |

### Rendering Issues

| Issue | Fix Pattern |
|-------|-------------|
| Missing key prop | Add unique key to list items |
| Conditional rendering bugs | Add proper checks before rendering |
| Rendering null/undefined | Add fallback or default values |
| CSS class inconsistencies | Use consistent class naming patterns |
| SVG rendering issues | Add proper SVG attributes and viewBox |

### Performance Issues

| Issue | Fix Pattern |
|-------|-------------|
| Excessive re-renders | Use React.memo, useCallback, useMemo |
| Large component size | Split into smaller components |
| Expensive calculations | Move to useMemo hook |
| Frequent state updates | Batch state updates |
| Render optimization | Implement virtualization for long lists |

### State Management Issues

| Issue | Fix Pattern |
|-------|-------------|
| Stale closures | Use functional updates |
| Missing effect dependencies | Add all required dependencies |
| Prop drilling | Use context or composition |
| Complex state logic | Extract to custom hooks |
| Race conditions | Use cleanup functions in effects |

### Accessibility Issues

| Issue | Fix Pattern |
|-------|-------------|
| Missing ARIA attributes | Add proper role, aria-* attributes |
| Keyboard navigation | Add keyboard event handlers |
| Color contrast | Adjust colors for proper contrast |
| Focus management | Implement proper focus handling |
| Screen reader compatibility | Add proper alt text and labels |

## Testing Component Fixes

### Unit Test Fixes

```typescript
// Add or fix component unit tests
edit_file("front-end/src/components/__tests__/[ComponentName].test.tsx",
          "Fix component unit tests",
          "import React from 'react';
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';
import { [ComponentName] } from '../[ComponentName]';

describe('[ComponentName]', () => {
  // Fixed: Test with required props
  test('renders correctly with required props', () => {
    render(<[ComponentName] data={[]} options={{}} />);
    expect(screen.getByRole('region')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  // Fixed: Test conditional rendering
  test('renders items when provided', () => {
    const testData = [
      { id: '1', name: 'Item 1', value: 10 },
      { id: '2', name: 'Item 2', value: 20 },
    ];
    
    render(<[ComponentName] data={testData} options={{}} />);
    expect(screen.getAllByRole('listitem')).toHaveLength(2);
    expect(screen.getByText('Item 1')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  // Fixed: Test interaction handling
  test('calls onSelect when item is clicked', () => {
    const handleSelect = jest.fn();
    const testData = [{ id: '1', name: 'Item 1', value: 10 }];
    
    render(
      <[ComponentName] 
        data={testData} 
        options={{}}
        onSelect={handleSelect}
      />
    );
    
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Item 1'));
    expect(handleSelect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('1');
  });
});")
```

### Integration Test Fixes

```typescript
// Add or fix component integration tests
edit_file("front-end/src/tests/integration/[feature].test.tsx",
          "Fix component integration tests",
          "import React from 'react';
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { [ParentComponent] } from 'components/[ParentComponent]';
import { AppProvider } from 'contexts/AppContext';

describe('[Feature] Integration', () => {
  // Fixed: Test component integration with parent
  test('integrates with parent component correctly', async () => {
    render(
      <AppProvider>
        <[ParentComponent] />
      </AppProvider>
    );
    
    // Verify child component rendered within parent
    expect(screen.getByTestId('child-component')).toBeInTheDocument();
    
    // Test interaction between components
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Trigger Action'));
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByText('Action Result')).toBeInTheDocument();
    });
  });
});")
```

